  "name": "Rope Combatant",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/control/debuff-chains-ropes-blue.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you wield a 10ft length of rope as an improvised weapon, it gains the finesse and reach property, much like a whip, and deals your choice of 1d6 bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage. You can alternatively use a 10ft length of rope like a net.</p>\n<p>If you are armed with a Strong Rope, you gain a bonus to attack and damage rolls with it equal to half your proficiency bonus, rounded up. When you use a Strong Rope like a net, the hit points and escape DC are the same as the Strong Rope.</p>",
